{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hardware test input template\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy `test_labjack_device.ipynb.template` to `test_labjack_device.ipynb` before editing or running it. The working notebook is ignored by Git. If it already exists, keep that file rather than overwriting its inputs or outputs.\n",
    "\n",
    "Replace every all-capital placeholder before running this notebook. Values are passed directly to the project enums and LJM so malformed inputs retain their native errors.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `<DEVICE_TYPE>`: a `LabJackDeviceTypeEnum` member name\n",
    "- `<CONNECTION_TYPE>`: a `LabJackConnectionTypeEnum` member name\n",
    "- `<DEVICE_IDENTIFIER>`: the selected device identifier\n",
    "- `<AIN_CHANNEL_1>`, `<AIN_CHANNEL_2>`: the physically connected AIN names"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Connection\n",
    "\n",
    "The connection stays open across cells. Call `lj_device.close()` when finished; the registered `atexit` callback also attempts to close it on normal Python process exit. Closing the notebook tab or interrupting a cell does not invoke that callback."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import atexit\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "from pylabjack import (\n",
    "    LabJackConnectionTypeEnum,\n",
    "    LabJackDevice,\n",
    "    LabJackDeviceTypeEnum,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "DEVICE_TYPE = LabJackDeviceTypeEnum[\"<DEVICE_TYPE>\"]\n",
    "CONNECTION_TYPE = LabJackConnectionTypeEnum[\"<CONNECTION_TYPE>\"]\n",
    "DEVICE_IDENTIFIER = \"<DEVICE_IDENTIFIER>\"\n",
    "\n",
    "lj_device = LabJackDevice(\n",
    "    device_type=DEVICE_TYPE,\n",
    "    connection_type=CONNECTION_TYPE,\n",
    "    device_identifier=DEVICE_IDENTIFIER,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(type(lj_device))\n",
    "print(lj_device)\n",
    "\n",
    "atexit.register(lj_device.close)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## On-demand read and write\n",
    "\n",
    "These examples use the connection opened above and return a `ReadWrite` operation object. Select scalar numeric registers supported by your device.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Single read\n",
    "\n",
    "Replace `<READ_REGISTER>` with one readable register or channel name. `.value` gives the single read result."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "READ_REGISTER = \"<READ_REGISTER>\"\n",
    "\n",
    "single_read = lj_device.read(READ_REGISTER)\n",
    "print(type(single_read))\n",
    "print(single_read)\n",
    "print(single_read.value)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Consecutive readings:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "read_num = 10\n",
    "reads = np.full(read_num, np.nan)\n",
    "for i in range(read_num):\n",
    "    single_read = lj_device.read(READ_REGISTER)\n",
    "    reads[i] = single_read.value\n",
    "\n",
    "print(reads)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "ax.plot(reads)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Index\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(f\"Readings (V)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"Readings from {READ_REGISTER}\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Consecutive multi-register readings and plot.\n",
    "READ_CHANNELS = [\"AIN0\", \"AIN1\", \"AIN2\"]\n",
    "read_num = 10\n",
    "multi_reads = np.full((read_num, len(READ_CHANNELS)), np.nan)\n",
    "for i in range(read_num):\n",
    "    multi_read = lj_device.read(READ_CHANNELS)\n",
    "    multi_reads[i, :] = multi_read.values\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "for channel, values in zip(READ_CHANNELS, multi_reads.T):\n",
    "    ax.plot(values, label=channel, alpha=0.5)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Index\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Readings (V)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"Readings from {', '.join(READ_CHANNELS)}\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Single write\n",
    "\n",
    "Replace `<WRITE_REGISTER>` and `<WRITE_VALUE>` with a writable register and a finite numeric value appropriate for your electrical setup. Running this cell changes that register. `.written_values` contains the requested write value, not a readback."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "WRITE_REGISTER = \"<WRITE_REGISTER>\"\n",
    "WRITE_VALUE = float(\"<WRITE_VALUE>\")\n",
    "\n",
    "single_write = lj_device.write(WRITE_REGISTER, WRITE_VALUE)\n",
    "print(single_write)\n",
    "print(single_write.written_values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Stream"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Stream In"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "INPUT_CHANNELS = [\"<AIN_CHANNEL_1>\", \"<AIN_CHANNEL_2>\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "stream = lj_device.stream(\n",
    "    scan_rate_Hz=25e3,\n",
    "    duration_s=2,\n",
    "    inputs={\"channels\": INPUT_CHANNELS},\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(stream)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "total_nans = np.sum([np.isnan(value['V']).sum() for value in stream.records.values()])\n",
    "print(f\"Recounting skipped total samples = {total_nans}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10,4))\n",
    "n_skip_head = 100\n",
    "for channel, record in stream.records.items():\n",
    "    ax.plot(record[\"t\"][n_skip_head:], record[\"V\"][n_skip_head:], label=channel)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Time [s]\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Voltage [V]\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"LabJack Stream Data\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Stream Out"
   ]
  },
